[node name="TutorialText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="TutorialModal/TutorialPanel/ScrollContainer" unique_id=1493955337]
custom_minimum_size = Vector2(700, 0)
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_vertical = 3
theme_override_colors/default_color = Color(0.85, 0.86, 0.9, 1)
theme_override_fonts/normal_font = ExtResource("3_mech_font")
theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 18
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][font_size=24][color=#f3c23b]TUI RULES & BASICS[/color][/font_size][/center]

[color=#b0b2b8]TUI is a fast-paced card game themed around Chinese Chess pieces. It features unique tactical play, hand matching, and the legendary \"Perfect\" strategy.[/color]

---

[font_size=20][color=#e54e4e]1. THE CARDS[/color][/font_size]
The deck consists of [b]32 cards[/b] in total, split into [color=#ff5555]Red[/color] and [color=#555555]Black[/color] (16 cards each).
Red cards always beat Black cards of the same rank.

[b]Ranks & Quantities per color:[/b]
• [b]General[/b] (aka King) - 1 unit
• [b]Advisor[/b] (aka Plane) - 2 units
• [b]Elephant[/b] - 2 units
• [b]Rook[/b] (aka Boat) - 2 units
• [b]Horse[/b] - 2 units
• [b]Cannon[/b] (aka House) - 2 units
• [b]Soldier[/b] (aka Chip) - 5 units

[b]Card Power Hierarchy (Highest to Lowest):[/b]
[color=#ffdd55]Red General > Black General > Red Advisor > Black Advisor > ... > Red Soldier > Black Soldier[/color]

---

[font_size=20][color=#e54e4e]2. GAMEPLAY FLOW[/color][/font_size]
• [b]Players:[/b] 4 players, each dealt [b]8 cards[/b] at random.
• [b]Leader:[/b] One player starts as Leader and plays a card or set.
• [b]Play Types:[/b] All players must follow the Leader's chosen play type:
  - [b]Single:[/b] Any single card.
  - [b]Pair:[/b] Two cards of the [i]same character AND same color[/i] (e.g. Red Advisor + Red Advisor).
  - [b]Noble Set:[/b] 3 to 6 cards of the same color, forming a group.
    - [i]Royal Noble:[/i] General + Advisor + Elephant (max 5 cards)
    - [i]War Noble:[/i] Rook + Horse + Cannon (max 6 cards)
    - (Duplicates are allowed, e.g., General + Advisor + Advisor + Elephant)
  - [b]Soldier Set:[/b] 3 to 5 Soldiers of the same color.
• [b]Winning turns:[/b] The highest card/set wins the turn, collects all cards played, and becomes the new Leader.

---

[font_size=20][color=#e54e4e]3. FOLDING & TACTICS[/color][/font_size]
• If you cannot follow the play type or wish to save cards, you must [b]Fold[/b].
• Folding players choose the required number of cards to discard, which go to the turn winner.
• [b]Perfect Tactic:[/b] If you win 7 consecutive turns from the start, your 8th and last card is a [color=#ffdd55]Black Soldier[/color], it beats ANY card (even the General!).

---

[font_size=20][color=#e54e4e]4. SCORING[/color][/font_size]
At the end of a round, score points based on won cards:
[b]Score = (Total Won Cards) ÷ 4[/b]. Maximum is 8 points per round!"

